  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/533E65">Definition <span data-tag="533E65">5.5.6.8</span>.</a>$k$-truncated!map between Kan complexestruncated!map between Kan complexes$k$-truncated!morphism in an $\infty $-categorytruncated!morphism in an $\infty $-category We will say that a map $f: X \rightarrow Y$ of Kan complexes is <em>$k$-truncated</em> if the homotopy fibers of $f$ (taken over any base point of $Y$) are $k$-truncated. We will say that a morphism $f: C \rightarrow D$ in an arbitrary $\infty $-category $\calC $ is <em>$k$-truncated</em> if composition with $f$ induces a $k$-truncated map $\bHom _{\calC }(E,C) \rightarrow \bHom _{\calC }(E,D)$ for every object $E \in \calC $. </p>
